  "summary": "Proves that 2-adic carry recurrences and polynomial dictionaries D of moves fail to connect modular subset sum fibers at linear depth k = alpha n. Every residue-conserving relation vector has Hamming weight w >= Omega(n / log n), forcing Boolean admissibility to decay as 2^-Omega(n / log n). Consequently, the average graph degree collapses to 0, isolated vertices dominate (fraction >= 1 - 2^-Omega(n / log n) -> 1), and the global spectral gap is identically 0.",
  "pillars": {
    "pillar_1_carry_recurrence_identity": "sum (a_i mod 2^k) x_i = (t mod 2^k) + 2^k c_k(x) identically over Z, with c_k(x) in [0, m-1] carrying at most log2(m) = O(log n) bits of entropy.",
    "pillar_2_quotient_entropy_barrier": "H(x | c_k(x)) >= (1 - alpha)n - log2(m) = Omega(n) bits, proving carry quotienting leaves exponential entropy intact.",
    "pillar_3_birthday_volume_weight_bound": "W*(k, m) = floor((k - lambda) / log2(2 e m)) = Omega(n / log n), proving no non-zero relations exist below W* with probability 1 - 2^-Omega(n).",
    "pillar_4_boolean_admissibility_decay": "P_adm <= 2^-W* + 1 = 2^-Omega(n / log n) on fiber assignments.",
    "pillar_5_graph_fragmentation_barrier": "d_bar <= n^C 2^-Omega(n / log n) -> 0; V_iso / |F_k| >= 1 - 2^-Omega(n / log n) -> 1; spectral gap vanishes and random-to-target reachability is identically zero."
  },
